      "citations": null,
      "text": "This builds HML from the value-weighted monthly block of `6_Portfolios_2x3.csv`: HML = 0.5 \u00d7 (Small Hi-BM + Big Hi-BM) \u2212 0.5 \u00d7 (Small Lo-BM + Big Lo-BM), the same construction Ken French uses. The script parses only the first \"Average Value Weighted Returns -- Monthly\" block, maps missing codes (-99.99, -999) to NaN, and drops any month where a required portfolio is missing.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\ndef main():\n    fname = \"6_Portfolios_2x3.csv\"\n    with open(fname, encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        lines = f.read().splitlines()\n\n    # Locate the monthly value-weighted block\n    start = None\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        if \"average value weighted returns\" in line.lower() and \"monthly\" in line.lower():\n            start = i\n            break\n    if start is None:\n        # fallback: first line that begins with a YYYYMM date\n        for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n            if re.match(r\"^\\s*\\d{6}\\s*,\", line):\n                start = i - 1\n                break\n    if start is None:\n        raise SystemExit(\"Could not find monthly value-weighted block\")\n\n    date_re = re.compile(r\"^\\d{6}$\")\n    rows = []\n    started = False\n    for line in lines[start + 1:]:\n        s = line.strip()\n        if not s:\n            if started:\n                break\n            continue\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in s.split(\",\")]\n        if date_re.match(parts[0]) and len(parts) >= 7:\n            started = True\n            vals = []\n            for p in parts[1:7]:\n                try:\n                    v = float(p)\n                except ValueError:\n                    v = np.nan\n                if v != v or v == -99.99 or v == -999.0:\n                    v = np.nan\n                vals.append(v)\n            rows.append((int(parts[0]), vals))\n        else:\n            if started:\n                break\n\n    # Column order in file: SMALL LoBM, ME1 BM2, SMALL HiBM, BIG LoBM, ME2 BM2, BIG HiBM\n    df = pd.DataFrame(\n        [r[1] for r in rows],\n        index=[r[0] for r in rows],\n        columns=[\"SL\", \"SM\", \"SH\", \"BL\", \"BM\", \"BH\"],\n    )\n    df.index.name = \"date\"\n\n    hml = 0.5 * (df[\"SH\"] + df[\"BH\"]) - 0.5 * (df[\"SL\"] + df[\"BL\"])\n    out = pd.DataFrame({\"date\": df.index.astype(int), \"value\": hml.values})\n    out = out.dropna(subset=[\"value\"])\n    out[\"date\"] = out[\"date\"].astype(int)\n    out.to_csv(\"output.csv\", index=False, columns=[\"date\", \"value\"])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
